<title>UK: CRICKET-NATWEST TROPHY SECOND ROUND RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-NATWEST TROPHY SECOND ROUND RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of NatWest Trophy (60</p>
<p>overs) second round cricket matches on Wednesday:</p>
<p>At Derby: Derybshire beat Northamptonshire by 144 runs.</p>
<p>Derbyshire 324-7 innings closed (K.Barnett 111, C.Adams 101).</p>
<p>Northamptonshire 180 (A.Penberthy 62, J.Snape 54; D.Malcolm</p>
<p>7-35).</p>
<p>At Chelmsford: Essex beat Worcestershire by seven wickets.</p>
<p>Worcestershire 286-9 innings closed (G.Hick 146). Essex 287-3</p>
<p>(S.Law 100, A.Grayson 82 not out, R.Irani 79 not out).</p>
<p>At Southampton: Glamorgan beat Hampshire by two wickets.</p>
<p>Hampshire 302-6 innings closed (R.Smith 119). Glamorgan 304-8</p>
<p>(A. Dale 71, S.James 69, H.Morris 53).</p>
<p>At Leicester: Yorkshire beat Leicestershire by 128 runs.</p>
<p>Yorkshire 310-5 innings closed (C.White 96 not out,M.Moxon 74,</p>
<p>B. Parker 69). Leicestershire 182 (I.Sutcliffe 90; R.Stemp</p>
<p>4-54).</p>
<p>At Uxbridge: Middlesex beat Gloucestershire by four wickets.</p>
<p>Gloucestershire 277-9 innings closed (M.Lynch 100; J.Kallis</p>
<p>4-47). Middlesex 280-6 (J.Kallis 100, J.Pooley 79 not out).</p>
<p>At The Oval: Nottinghamshire beat Surrey by 22 runs.</p>
<p>Nottinghamshnire 176 (N.Astle 56) v Surrey 154.</p>
<p>At Hove: Sussex beat Lancashire by seven wickets. Lancashire</p>
<p>283-6 innings closed (J.Crawley 113 not out, I.Austin 97).</p>
<p>Sussex 286-3 (K.Greenfield 129, M.Newell 75 not out).</p>
<p>At Edgbaston: Warwickshire beat Somerset by 11 runs.</p>
<p>Warwickshire 220 (D.Ostler 54). Somerset 209 (S.Ecclestone 87).</p>
</text>
